      "sketch": "Convert the class to a frozen dataclass and expose the data attributes directly. Keep only the behaviour method `is_premium`.\n```python\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Customer:\n    customer_id: int\n    name: str\n    email: str\n    tier: str = \"standard\"\n\n    def is_premium(self) -> bool:\n        return self.tier == \"premium\"\n```\nRemove the explicit getter methods (`customer_id`, `name`, `email`, `tier`). Callers can now access `customer.customer_id` etc., while the class remains immutable and cohesive."
